    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_330bfa11",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person holding an ancient artifact, with overlaid text that reads 'black people' and 'anything thoat doesn't belong to them.' This juxtaposition is a racist trope that implies Black people are inherently entitled to nothing, suggesting they are not the rightful owners of cultural or historical artifacts. The meme uses dehumanizing and derogatory language to attack Black people based on their race, fitting the definition of hateful content as it directly targets a protected characteristic (race) with offensive and discriminatory messaging. The visual of the artifact being held by a person (who is not Black) reinforces the stereotype that Black people are not connected to or entitled to such cultural heritage, which is a form of racialized historical erasure and appropriation. The meme's intent is to spread racist ideology by associating Black people with a lack of ownership or legitimacy over cultural artifacts, which is a harmful and hateful message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_cb79fdb7"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
