      "label": "display_of_antique_artifact",
      "description": "A woman is holding an ancient goblet artifact, which is placed on a black pedestal. The artifact is the central focus of the scene, with the woman positioned behind it, slightly out of focus. Overlaid text labels the woman as 'black people' and the artifact as 'anything thoat doesn't belong to them', indicating a hateful context. The spatial arrangement emphasizes the artifact as the primary subject, with the woman serving as a contextual figure.",
